        name: "omni_reference_task_type",
        kind: "enum",
        label: "Omni Reference Task Type",
        required: false,
        description:
          "Subtask hint. Omni reference tasks cover three subtasks - reference-to-video, video editing, and video extension. Leave it unset - equivalent to the upstream default 'auto' - to let the model infer the subtask from the reference media and prompt, in which case an incompatible parameter surfaces as an asynchronous task failure. Setting an explicit subtask has its constraints validated when the task is submitted instead, so a bad request is rejected up front and no task is created. 'reference' generates a new video from reference images/videos/audio and puts no extra constraints on ratio or duration. 'edit' edits an existing video and requires exactly one reference_videos entry of 4-30s, ratio 'adaptive', and duration -1. 'extend' extends an existing video and requires exactly one reference_videos entry and ratio 'adaptive'. The explicit values apply only to requests that carry reference media - the upstream model rejects them on prompt-only, first-frame, and first+last-frame requests, so leave the field unset for those. The model still re-derives the task type from the prompt while processing, so a prompt that disagrees with the value you set still fails the task asynchronously. This property is only available through the API.",
